Hierarchical Multi-Label Text Classification with Silver Labels and Selective LLM Refinement
This repository contains the implementation of a hierarchical multi-label text classification (HMTC) system. The task involves assigning review documents to a single valid taxonomy path prefix—either root-parent or root-parent-leaf—within a directed acyclic taxonomy of 531 product classes.

Overview
Due to the absence of gold-labeled training data, this project employs a weakly-supervised pipeline:
+1


Silver Labeling: Generating high-confidence pseudo-labels via hybrid semantic-lexical retrieval.
+4


Taxonomy-Aware Training: Training a Dual-Encoder (SBERT + GNN) model with structural constraints.
+2


Selective LLM Refinement: Enhancing predictions for ambiguous samples using a budgeted LLM strategy.

System Architecture
1. Silver Label Generation (silver_labeler.py)
To bootstrap the model, we generate "Silver Labels" for the training corpus.


Hybrid Retrieval: We combine SBERT (semantic context) and BM25 (lexical keyword matching) to compute document-class similarity.
+2


Path Restoration: Top-K leaf candidates are restored to full root-to-leaf paths using the taxonomy.


Sibling-Normalized Probability: A softmax-based decision determines whether to stop at the parent level or include the leaf based on its relative confidence among siblings.

2. Model Architecture (model.py)
The classifier is a Dual-Encoder designed to jointly represent documents and taxonomy classes.


Document Encoder: A frozen pretrained Transformer (BERT) with mean-pooling to extract review embeddings.
+1


Class Encoder (GNN): A Graph Convolutional Network that refines class embeddings by passing messages across the taxonomy graph.
+1

Loss Functions:


Taxonomy-Aware BCE: Multi-label loss with masking to ignore non-selected siblings of a positive parent.
+2


Supervised Contrastive Loss: Adds a projection head to cluster documents sharing similar labels in the embedding space.

3. Selective LLM Refinement (trainer.py)
At inference time, we utilize a "Selective Refinement" strategy to optimize accuracy within a strict API budget.


Uncertainty Estimation: The model calculates an uncertainty score using the Margin (score difference between the top-2 paths) and the Leaf Gap (closeness to the inclusion threshold).
+2


Budgeted Selection: Only the top-N most uncertain samples (e.g., 10,000 items) are sent to Gemini-2.5-Flash.


Narrowed Candidate Prompting: The LLM is provided with a truncated review and only 2 candidate paths, choosing between parent-only or specific leaf nodes.


Results
Method Variant	Kaggle Score (Micro-F1)
Node-wise prediction (no constraints)	
0.37 

Path-prefix formulation + Constrained decoding	
0.53 

Selective LLM leaf-only refinement (Final)	

0.60
The implementation achieved significant performance gains by enforcing the single-path nature of product categories.
